  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The table below provides the potential difference <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> and the plate separation <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span> for four different uniform electric field regions.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Region</th><th>Potential difference / <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\mathrm{V}\"></span></th><th>Separation / <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\mathrm{mm}\"></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>P</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\"></span></td></tr><tr><td>Q</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"150\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10.0\"></span></td></tr><tr><td>R</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\"></span></td></tr><tr><td>S</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"300\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20.0\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>In which region is the magnitude of the electric field strength the greatest?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Region P</li><li data-label=\"B\">Region Q</li><li data-label=\"C\">Region R</li><li data-label=\"D\">Region S</li></ol>"
